## 0. Headline verdict — BLOCKER IS DEEPER THAN A ONE-LINE CONSTANT

GOAL NOT MET under the stated constraint: falkon's first paint is NOT
achievable by changing only `CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_*` in
`capability_space_sel4.h`. The task's specified one-line patch
(`CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND` 7→9, "64×512 = 32768 slots") DOES NOT BOOT.
Root cause is fully diagnosed below with empirical proof and the seL4
kernel's own error messages. The vendored tree has been reverted to
pristine; no patch is applied; no ledger row is added. This log is the
deliverable per the task's explicit guidance: "If a NEW blocker
appears, capture the exact stage and report (no silent hang)."

The new blocker is NOT a falkon problem and NOT a caps-quota problem.
It is a base-sel4 architectural coupling: every child-PD CNode is
backed by exactly ONE 4 KiB untyped page, which hard-caps each CNode
at 2^7 = 128 slots (seL4 CTE = 32 bytes), and therefore caps the
total per-PD CSpace at 2^(1ST+2ND) ≤ 2^(7+7) = 16384. Falkon needs
strictly more than 16384, so NO single-line change to
`capability_space_sel4.h` can satisfy it. Growing further requires a
multi-file base-sel4 rearchitecture (populate the 8K/16K untyped
pools + rewire the `Cnode` backing + `untyped_sel`), which is outside
the "ONLY the one-line cspace patch" constraint.

Acceptance (1) falkon_probe PASS: NOT MET (blocked, root cause proven).
Acceptance (2) fixture GET: NOT MET (falkon dies before HTTP GET).
Acceptance (3) 5 regression scenarios PASS: MET (run at the maximal
  single-page-compatible cspace config 16384, all 5 pass — proving a
  global cspace enlargement is regression-clean; see §5).
Acceptance (4) docs/11 ledger entry: NOT ADDED — the patch is not
  viable, so per AGENTS.md §5.2 no ledger row is recorded. The
  finding lives here instead.
Acceptance (5) this evidence file: MET.

