## 1. The hypothesis (from the task / commit bae5423d1b)

P4 (bae5423d1b) proved falkon boots FROM DISK (image.elf 12 MiB,
508 MiB payload on the GENODE partition via rom_pkg; ldso resolves the
237 MiB libQt6WebEngineCore.lib.so from disk; lwIP DHCPs to
10.0.2.15) but dies before first paint:

    out of selector  →  denied RM-session  (ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2)

Diagnosed in bae5423d1b / docs/evidence/p4-falkon-disk.log §3 as the
FIXED 8192-slot per-child-PD CNode:

    capability_space_sel4.h:
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST = 6   (64 1st-level slots)
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND = 7   (128 slots per 2nd-level CNode, 64-bit)
      CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2     = 13  →  2^13 = 8192 slots per child PD

The task's approved remedy: raise `CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND` 7→9 so the
per-PD CSpace becomes 2^(6+9) = 32768. This file records what happens
when that is applied.

