## 2. ATTEMPT 1 — the specified patch (2ND 7→9) DOES NOT BOOT

Patch applied (single source confirmed — every other reference,
`platform_pd.cc:172,206`, `platform_pd.h:64,138,159`,
`capability_space.cc:61,159,167,189`, derives from the three
`CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2*` constants; the `7` appears only in the ternary):

    - CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND = (CONFIG_WORD_SIZE == 32) ? 8 : 7,
    + CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND = (CONFIG_WORD_SIZE == 32) ? 8 : 9,

Rebuilt cleanly (`capability_space.o`, `platform_pd.o`, `core/sel4/core`
all recompiled; no compile error). Booted
`run/sponge-falkon-disk KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc RUN_OPT=--include image/disk`.
Log: docs/evidence/p4-falkon-cspace-run.log

FAILURE — core cannot construct the FIRST child PD. The boot dies
IMMEDIATELY after the banner, before any `[init -> ...]` line:

    Genode 26.05
    5809 MiB RAM and 523288 caps assigned to init
    Error: seL4_Untyped_RetypeAtOffset (cnode) returned 10
    Error: Cnode construction failed
    <<seL4 ... Untyped Retype: Insufficient memory
       (1 * 16384 bytes needed, 4096 bytes available).>>
    ... (repeats for every 2nd-level CNode core tries to create) ...
    Warning: copy: seL4_CNode_Copy (...) returned 6
    Warning: with_cspace_cnode invalid sel
    vm fault on code at address 0xf1fe0 ...  ->  Test execution timed out

seL4 error 10 = seL4_NotEnoughMemory. The kernel needs 16384 bytes to
retype one 2^9-slot CNode but the backing untyped only has 4096.

================================================================

## 3. ROOT CAUSE — single-page CNode backing (the coupling the
           task's model missed)

### 3.1 seL4 CTE size = 32 bytes (measured from the kernel)

The kernel's own accounting: a CNode of `size_bits = 9` (the value we
set) needs `2^9 slots × 32 bytes = 16384 bytes`. Therefore each seL4
capability-table entry (CTE) is 32 bytes on this 64-bit build.

### 3.2 Genode backs each child-PD CNode with exactly ONE 4 KiB page

`genode/repos/base-sel4/src/core/include/cnode.h` (Cnode ctor, the
4-arg `Range_allocator` variant used by `platform_pd.cc:170,204`):

    Cnode(Cap_sel parent_sel, Index dst_idx, uint8_t size_log2,
          Range_allocator &phys_alloc)
    :
        Cnode_base(dst_idx, size_log2),
        _phys(Untyped_memory::alloc_page(phys_alloc))   <-- ONE page
    {
        _phys.with_result([&](auto &res) {
            auto const service =
                Untyped_memory::untyped_sel(addr_t(res.ptr)).value(); <-- 4K untyped
            ok = create<Cnode_kobj>(service, parent_sel, dst_idx, size_log2);
        }, ...);
    }

`Untyped_memory::alloc_page` → `alloc_pages(phys, 1)` → exactly one
`PAGE_SIZE` (4096) byte region (`untyped_memory.h`). And
`untyped_sel()` always returns a `TOP_CNODE_UNTYPED_4K` selector
(4 KiB untyped cap). seL4 cannot retype a 4096-byte untyped into a
16384-byte object → error 10.

### 3.3 The hard cap

A 4 KiB page holds `4096 / 32 = 128 = 2^7` CTEs. So BOTH
`CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST` and `CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND` are individually
capped at 7 by the single-page backing. The maximal single-page-
compatible per-PD CSpace is therefore

    2^(CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST + CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND) ≤ 2^(7+7) = 16384.

Upstream's `1ST=6, 2ND=7` (8192) sits below this cap. The task's
`2ND=9` (4-page CNodes) breaks it. This is NOT a coincidence: the
upstream value is precisely the largest 2nd-level CNode that fits in
one 4 KiB page at the seL4 CTE size.

### 3.4 Why the 8K/16K untyped pools don't rescue it

`Core_cspace` DOES define 4K/8K/16K untyped CNode slots
(`TOP_CNODE_UNTYPED_4K/8K/16K`, core_cspace.h). But
`Platform::_init_allocators` populates ONLY the 4K pool
(platform.cc:113 — the single `turn_into_untyped_object` call targets
`TOP_CNODE_UNTYPED_4K`). `Untyped_memory` exposes no allocator for
8K/16K untypeds and `untyped_sel()` always returns a 4K selector. So
backing a >4 KiB CNode would require, at minimum:

  (a) platform.cc: also `turn_into_untyped_object(... UNTYPED_8K/16K ...)`
      for general RAM (and decide a sizing policy),
  (b) untyped_memory.h: an `untyped_sel(phys, size_log2)` that selects
      the right pool, and
  (c) cnode.h: allocate `2^(Cnode_kobj::SIZE_LOG2 + size_log2 - PAGE_SIZE_LOG2)`
      pages and obtain a single covering untyped cap.

That is a multi-file base-sel4 rearchitecture, explicitly outside the
"ONLY the one-line cspace patch" constraint.

