## 4. ATTEMPT 2 — maximal single-page config (1ST=7, 2ND=7 = 16384)

To prove the cap is real AND to measure whether 16384 (the most a
one-line change can give) is enough for falkon, the largest single-
page-compatible config was tested:

    CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST = 7   (128 1st-level slots, 1 page)
    CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND = 7   (128 slots/2nd-level CNode, 1 page each)
    total = 2^14 = 16384 slots per child PD   (2× the upstream 8192)

Both levels fit in one 4 KiB page → the boot is single-page compatible.

BUILD/BOOT: clean. `make core` succeeded; the falkon-disk scenario
booted normally (no Cnode-construction errors, no seL4 error 10).
Log: docs/evidence/p4-falkon-16384.log

FALKON RESULT — still fails, at the SAME point as the original 8192
blocker, just with more headroom consumed first. Sequence:

    [init -> system -> falkon_probe] falkon-probe: [3] launch ok ...
    [init -> rom_pkg] Warning: flush page table entries - mapping cache
                         full - PD: init -> rom_pkg out of selector
    [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] lwIP Nic interface up
        address=10.0.2.15 ... gateway=10.0.2.2
    [init -> rom_pkg] out of selector      (repeats — rom_pkg caching
                                            the 508 MiB payload exceeds
                                            its 16384-slot CNode)
    [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] out of selector
    [init -> system -> pkg_runtime -> falkon] Error: stop because parent
        denied RM-session: label="", ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2
    [init -> system -> falkon_probe] falkon-probe: FAIL falkon window
        never rendered into nitpicker
    -> Test execution timed out (bounded, identified; no silent hang)

CONCLUSION: 16384 is INSUFFICIENT. Two PDs exhaust it independently:
  - rom_pkg (cached_fs_rom) caches falkon's 508 MiB payload as ROM
    sessions → many frame caps in rom_pkg's own PD.
  - falkon's WebEngine runtime (render buffers / qtwebengine_shm /
    many 4 KiB mappings) on top of the eagerly-mapped Qt6/WebEngine
    libs.

Since 16384 is the MAXIMUM any single-line `capability_space_sel4.h`
change can yield (§3.3), and it is insufficient, falkon's first paint
is NOT achievable under the stated constraint. Proven, not speculated.

