## 7. Options for the orchestrator (decision required)

The goal (falkon first paint on base-sel4) is achievable only by
relaxing the "one-line cspace patch" constraint. Ranked options:

  A. Relax the constraint; vendored multi-file base-sel4 patch.
     Populate the 8K/16K (and possibly a 2 MiB) untyped pools in
     platform.cc, add a size-aware `Untyped_memory::untyped_sel`, and
     make the `Cnode` ctor allocate `2^(5+size_log2-12)` pages with a
     single covering untyped. Then set e.g. 1ST=7, 2ND=11
     (128 × 2048 = 262144 slots) — comfortably above WebEngine's need.
     Record TWO ledger rows (cspace + cnode/untyped). Risk: non-trivial
     base-sel4 internals change; needs careful review; verify falkon
     actually paints AND the full regression set still passes. The
     8K/16K CNode slots already existing in Core_cspace is evidence
     upstream anticipated this direction.

  B. Switch falkon to base-hw for the seL4-media product.
     base-hw has no fixed per-PD CSpace (it is quota-driven). docs/14
     §9 locks base-hw out for the Alpha media; that section would need
     revisiting. Larger strategic change, out of scope for a patch.

  C. Accept falkon-on-sel4 as blocked for Alpha; ship the disk-based
     payload architecture (PROVEN in P4/bae5423d1b — falkon boots from
     disk, loads WebEngine, DHCPs) and document that first paint needs
     either (A) or a kernel with a larger per-PD CSpace. Update
     docs/14 §11 risk 3 to record that the limiter is the single-page
     CNode backing (NOT merely the 8192 constant), and that the caps
     quota is doubly moot.

  D. (Optional intermediate, regression-clean per §5) apply the
     maximal single-line config 1ST=7 (= 16384) as a strict 2×
     improvement. It does NOT unblock falkon but helps any workload in
     the 8192–16384 band and is a one-line, regression-clean patch.
     Only worth taking if (A) is deferred.

Recommended next step: decide between (A) and (C). If (A), the work
breaks down as the three sub-changes in (A) plus a re-run of
sponge-falkon-disk and the §5 regression set.

